<!--Render Target Documentation — FqnNaming
  FQN: com.machineblocks.bml.target.render.documentation.FqnNaming-->
<rdoc:FqnNaming xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:rdoc="com.machineblocks.bml.target.render.documentation">

  <baseType>
    core:Documentation
  </baseType>
  <is>
    FQN to SCAD module name and file path
  </is>
  <documentation>
    Every MBOM block class is identified by its definition FQN. This target
    maps that FQN to a manifestation FQN, then to a module name and a file path.
    The mapping is a MachineBlocks convention, not a BlockML platform rule.
    Other targets do not replace a bml segment and do not emit one file per block.

    Automatic mapping applies when targetOptions omit sourcePackage and
    targetPackage. Split the FQN on "." and replace the one segment whose text
    is exactly bml with scad. The match is case-sensitive and segment-wide.
    mybml and bmlmodels are not bml. The replacement is not a substring search
    and does not prefer the first or last segment.

        Definition FQN:    com.machineblocks.bml.examples.Cross
        Manifestation FQN: com.machineblocks.scad.examples.Cross
        SCAD module:       mb__com__machineblocks__scad__examples__Cross
        Output file:       {srcDir}/com/machineblocks/scad/examples/Cross.scad

    Zero bml segments: MB_TARGET_PACKAGE_UNDETERMINED. The message names the
    source FQN and tells the caller to pass --target-package and, if needed,
    --source-package. More than one bml segment: MB_TARGET_PACKAGE_AMBIGUOUS.
    The message names the source FQN. Neither case writes a file.

    Explicit mapping applies when both sourcePackage and targetPackage are set.
    A definition FQN equal to the source package, or starting with that package
    plus a dot, keeps the remainder and swaps the root:

        sourcePackage com.example.models
        targetPackage com.example.scad
        com.example.models.bricks.MyBrick
          -> com.example.scad.bricks.MyBrick

    The bml-to-scad replacement is not applied on top. A selected block outside
    the source package is MB_SOURCE_OUTSIDE_ROOT. A referenced FQN outside the
    source package (an import or a child module) uses automatic mapping instead.
    If that automatic mapping fails, the compile fails and the host writes nothing.

    Preset JSON uses the same manifestation with extension .json.
    The output root is the configured blocks directory (srcDir), not a guessed
    dist, build, or scad directory.

    Name rules:

    - Segments separated by double underscore (__)
    - Packages lowercase
    - Class names PascalCase
    - Subclasses: additional PascalCase segment
    - Private helpers: __help__camelCase (not a block)
    - Private functions: __func__camelCase (not a block)

    Examples:

        com.machineblocks.bml.bricks.Standard
          -> mb__com__machineblocks__scad__bricks__Standard

        subclass Bottom of a manifested Wall
          -> mb__com__example__scad__Wall__Bottom

        private helper
          -> mb__com__example__scad__Wall__help__myHelper

        private function
          -> mb__com__example__scad__Wall__func__myFunc

    The names help and func are reserved and cannot be subclass names.

    Multiple block classes may share one SCAD file. The file is named after the
    primary class. The output root is srcDir.

  </documentation>
  <references>
    <see type="rdoc:Imports" relation="ReadNext" />
  </references>
</rdoc:FqnNaming>
